---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Eyebrow from "../components/Eyebrow.astro";

// Privacy policy for Jarvis, HNEC's internal finance application (Plaid production application, 9/25/26).
// Keep in step with the HNEC Information Security Policy (OneDrive: Haliburton NDT Engineering/Compliance/Plaid).
const EFFECTIVE = "September 25, 2026";

const sections = [
  {
    label: "Scope",
    body: [
      "Haliburton NDT Engineering Consultants, LLC (\"HNEC,\" \"we\") operates Jarvis, an internal application used only by the company's principal to keep his own business and household financial records: bookkeeping, tax records, deductions, and bills.",
      "Jarvis is not offered to the public or to customers. It has no user accounts for anyone else. This policy covers every piece of financial data Jarvis handles, including data received through Plaid.",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Data we collect",
    body: [
      "Through Plaid, with the account holder's authorization: account names, the last four digits of account numbers, balances, and transactions (date, amount, merchant, and category). Only Plaid's Transactions product is used.",
      "From Square: payments received by HNEC and the processing fees on them.",
      "We never receive or store bank usernames or passwords. They are entered only inside Plaid Link, Plaid's secure window. We do not collect full account or routing numbers, Social Security numbers, or any data about people other than the account holders.",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "How we use it",
    body: [
      "Only to produce the owner's own records: bookkeeping, tax preparation and deduction tracking, bill reminders, and private summaries.",
      "We do not sell, rent, or share this data. We do not use it for advertising, and we do not use it to make decisions about anyone.",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Consent",
    body: [
      "A bank account is connected only by its holder, through Plaid Link. Plaid Link shows Plaid's own consent screen and End User Privacy Policy before any data is shared. A joint account is connected only with the agreement of each co-owner.",
      "Consent can be withdrawn at any time by asking us to disconnect the account. We then revoke access at Plaid and delete the data as described under Retention and deletion.",
    ],
    link: { href: "https://plaid.com/legal/#end-user-privacy-policy", text: "Plaid End User Privacy Policy" },
  },
  {
    label: "Service providers",
    body: [
      "Plaid (connection to financial institutions) and Square (HNEC payments). Anthropic's Claude assistant, under the owner's own account, may process limited transaction details only to prepare the owner's private summaries. GitHub (source code only, no financial data) and Tailscale (encrypted private network).",
      "We disclose data to no one else, except where the law requires it.",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Security",
    body: [
      "Jarvis runs on a company-controlled computer and is not reachable from the internet. Data from Plaid is encrypted before it is stored (AES-256-GCM). Every connection uses TLS 1.2 or higher, or an encrypted private network.",
      "Every account that can reach the data requires multi-factor authentication. The systems are scanned for vulnerabilities every week.",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Retention and deletion",
    body: [
      "We keep these records as the owner's own business and household financial records, for as long as he uses them. There is no automatic deletion by age. Each year's policy review checks whether any records are no longer needed, and those are deleted. There are no backup copies of this data.",
      "When an account is disconnected, or if we stop using Plaid, access is revoked at Plaid and the stored access token is destroyed. Nothing more is collected from that account. Records already received are kept.",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Your choices",
    body: [
      "If your information is in an account connected to Jarvis (for example, a joint account), you can ask us what we hold, ask us to correct it, or ask us to delete it and disconnect the account. We respond within 30 days.",
    ],
  },
  {
    label: "Review and changes",
    body: [
      "We review this policy at least once a year, and whenever the way Jarvis handles data changes. The effective date above always shows the current version.",
    ],
  },
];
---
<Layout title="Jarvis Privacy Policy" description="Privacy policy for Jarvis, the internal finance application operated by Haliburton NDT Engineering Consultants, LLC." noindex>
  <section class="page-head shell">
    <Eyebrow number="00" label="Privacy policy" />
    <h1 class="page-head__h">Jarvis, our internal finance application.</h1>
    <p class="lead page-head__lead">
      What financial data Jarvis handles, why, who else touches it, how long we keep it, and how to have it deleted.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section shell">
    <dl class="dl record">
      <dt>Operator</dt><dd>Haliburton NDT Engineering Consultants, LLC · Denver, Colorado</dd>
      <dt>Application</dt><dd>Jarvis (internal, single user)</dd>
      <dt>Effective</dt><dd><span class="cred">{EFFECTIVE}</span></dd>
      <dt>Contact</dt><dd><a href="mailto:contact@haliburtonco.com">contact@haliburtonco.com</a></dd>
    </dl>
  </section>

  {sections.map((s, i) => (
    <section class="section shell policy">
      <Eyebrow number={String(i + 1).padStart(2, "0")} label={s.label} />
      <div class="policy__body">
        {s.body.map((p) => <p>{p}</p>)}
        {s.link && <p><a href={s.link.href} rel="noopener">{s.link.text}</a></p>}
      </div>
    </section>
  ))}
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-head { padding-block: clamp(4rem, 3rem + 6vw, 8rem) var(--space-6); }
  .page-head__h { margin-top: var(--space-4); max-width: 22ch; }
  .page-head__lead { margin-top: var(--space-5); }

  .record {
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .policy {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(10rem, 16rem) 1fr;
    align-items: start;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    padding-block: var(--space-5);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }
  .policy__body p + p { margin-top: var(--space-3); }

  @media (max-width: 720px) {
    .policy { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: var(--space-3); }
  }
</style>
